<p class="headlines"><br>
                Good for Your (Corporate) Health<br>
                <br>
                <span class="headlinebody">SYSPRO helps a personal health products company comply with stringent standards and track product.<br>
<br>
Natural Factors, located in Coquitlam, British Colombia, Canada, is a personal health products company that uses naturally sourced vitamins and minerals in such products as Echinamide, Chondroitin, and Glucosamine. These products can be distributed as capsules, tablets, or liquids. Natural Factors is well known for its research into different herbs and its work in introducing new and effective products into the expanding North American and global market of personal health products.<br>
<br>
An important aspect of what Natural Factors does is the control, monitoring, and obtaining of raw materials for its products. Natural Factors purchases many raw materials from suppliers all over the world. One of its largest suppliers is its wholly owned Factors Farms in Kelowna, British Columbia, Canada, where raw materials are grown in an organic, safe environment. <br>
<br>
When raw materials arrive at the facility, they undergo stringent goods inward inspection. Independent quality control tests are conducted to ensure a safe and effective end product. Once the tests are approved by the independent laboratories, Natural Factors verifies the tests once again to ensure optimum quality control standards. Upon passing both quality inspections, raw materials are dispensed and blended in state-of-the-art equipment. Such procedures help Natural Factors comply with Health Canada’s good manufacturing practice (GMP) and United States FDA requirements.<br>
<br>
Each month Natural Factors produces 70 million tablets and 80 million capsules. The company packs 70,000 bottles of 1,750 different finished goods product daily. On average, 300 sales orders are captured and 100 jobs are launched each day. There are 8,000 active stock items; new formulations are continually being introduced. Consequently, Natural Factors requires a software system that keeps pace with demand and ensures adherence to the various quality control measures throughout the manufacturing and distribution processes. <br>
<br>
Approximately 10 years ago, the decision was made to install a computerized system to help track inventory from raw material to distribution and assist with GMP compliance and financial tracking. At that time, Natural Factors chose SYSPRO because it matched the company’s needs and could grow with the company. Natural Factors started with the financial and inventory management application suite, then moved to manufacturing and MRP, and is now using the latest customer relationship management (CRM) product offering. <br>
<br>
SYSPRO has grown with Natural Factors as the company continues a 25 percent annual growth rate. The SYSPRO product has helped the company cope with the business pressures of increased volume due to increased demand and the continuous introduction of new products. It has also facilitated compliance with increasingly stringent GMP demands. <br>
<br>
How SYSPRO fits in<br>
As Natural Factors has grown, it has developed a corporate structure that includes five distribution centers, the Factors Farms for growing raw materials, and three different manufacturing facilities. SYSPRO helps the company manage product at each location as well as the movement of materials from one location to another. <br>
<br>
Demand for products comes from many sources. The company serves a wide variety of retail outlets and wholesale distributors. Customers may order a pallet load of one product or a bottle or two of a hundred products, depending on whether the retailer is a chain store or a corner store. Shipments occur three times a day. Product pricing and promotions are important aspects as a significant proportion of the products are seasonal. <br>
<br>
SYSPRO’s requirements planning module enables the five distribution companies to forecast demand and forward new orders to the various manufacturing facilities. Once an order is in a manufacturing facility, SYSPRO verifies all materials are present for the planned jobs before the actual jobs are issued to production and lot numbers assigned. If ingredients need to be purchased from suppliers (including Natural Factors’ own organic farm), SYSPRO automatically issues a purchase order.<br>
<br>
Within SYSPRO, features enable the tracking of multiple companies, multiple warehouses, and multiple bin locations. Computer terminals have been placed on the floor of Natural Factors facilities and even on the forklifts to ensure up-to-the-minute data integrity. The data track accounts and inventory levels as well as manufacturing processes, quality procedures, subcontractors, logistics operations, production planning and scheduling, and of course, customer service.<br>
<br>
SYSPRO’s distribution requirements planning (DRP) and material requirements planning (MRP) capability across multiple company environments coupled with the internal data tracking have enabled the company to effectively balance the supply chain and respond to changes as needed. <br>
<br>
The various inventory tracking capabilities of SYSPRO, coupled with a continuous improvement effort, have enabled the company, in the past year, to hold its inventory at approximately the same dollar value while growing revenues. This has had a noticeable impact on financial performance and enabled the company to maintain a double-digit growth rate. The information available to the users in the sales analysis screen shown in Figure 1, for example, enables users to quickly convey information to both customers and internal buyers.<br>
<br>
Figure 1<br>
<br>
Program environment<br>
Currently at Natural Factors a variety of computer technologies are employed. The SYSPRO software is installed in a two-tier client server environment using an IBM RISC server running AIX and Windows clients, which was recently updated to accommodate more than 100 active clients. The update has facilitated quick response times. <br>
<br>
A variety of computer networks are enabled at the company through wires, optical networks, wireless networks, and Citrix terminal client servers to several locations, including home-based over the Internet. This multi-network configuration provides for the deployment of SYSPRO where and when it is required. This flexibility has enabled the company to wire production facilities and receive real-time data from production. It also uses the data warehousing functionality within SYSPRO, which is based on SQL Server 2000, enabling the company to track trends and do data analysis as needed. <br>
<br>
SYSPRO has proven to be compatible with other applications. The database is complete and accessible through standard routines. The SYSPRO support and technical personnel know which technology is appropriate and regularly add to the software package functionality. It often seems like the simplest update adds the greatest business benefit.<br>
<br>
Ease of use and learning<br>
The SYSPRO interface is similar to the Windows Explorer functionality in terms of module structure, menu system, and navigation. However, users have the option of viewing menus as HTML pages or altering color patterns and creating their own workflow-structured menu environment including “fast menus,” favorites, a task list, and messaging. These features enable users at Natural Factors to create their own shortcuts to access frequently used SYSPRO functions and other applications. In addition, the SYSPRO browser has a built-in HTML viewer that can be used for viewing Web pages, reports, or other information.<br>
<br>
The screens are neatly designed and provide a great deal of data all in one location. Figure 2 shows an accounts receivable screen that displays both current and historical information about the customer’s payments, transactions, and check history. <br>
<br>
Figure 2<br>
<br>
Training is provided by the value-added reseller, Candlewest, that continues to provide assistance with ongoing projects. In addition, there is a user group in British Columbia and a Web site for SYSPRO users.<br>
<br>
Natural Factors is receiving greater benefit from the SYSPRO product as it adds on features like the CRM module. As the company expands, it is growing into the features of the product and finding ways to match business practices with the features in SYSPRO. <br>
<br>
SYSPRO has made tremendous improvements in the area of help, and Natural Factors now finds the assistance to be highly effective. In addition to extensive context sensitive online help, there are workbooks (for self-paced learning) and classroom-based workshops, as well as screen-cam presentations, which are self-running demonstrations on specific product features. These demonstrations enable users to see what they will be doing when the SYSPRO product is used. <br>
<br>
Natural Factors created its own standard operating procedures directly from the SYSPRO software and finds this an effective method of communicating across the disciplines and ensuring GMP. The company also makes extensive use of operator security, preferences, and defaults to guide personnel in using the standard software utilities of SYSPRO. <br>
<br>
The system has approximately a thousand configuration options that permit the use of the standard application in a wide variety of business applications. These are extremely useful in customizing the application functionality for each company. SYSPRO also has user defaults to further refine the application. Preferences by operator enable efficient use of the standard application. <br>
<br>
Also, the system has built-in messages to help operators perform their jobs correctly. SYSPRO advises the operator of error conditions such as insufficient stock, exceeded credit limit, insufficient margin, missing product class, and so on. The software puts the cursor directly into the appropriate position on the screen for the operator to take immediate action. This cuts down on errors and helps ensure data going into the system are correct. <br>
<br>
Best features<br>
At Natural Factors, SYSPRO provides communication across all its companies, and this is essential to Natural Factors’ effectiveness. Whether the question is about sales/forecasting or whether the company can supply product or how the cash flow looks or whether it is able to build an order, SYSPRO has that information available. Figure 3 shows a screen and a sample “what if” scenario for a particular work cell. <br>
<br>
Figure 3<br>
<br>
This full integration has enabled the company to do away with islands of information. The strength of SYSPRO for Natural Factors is its ability to handle information across the entire business environment, including finance, logistics, sales, planning, inventory, formulations, and laboratory. This broad company view gives Natural Factors one source of information that is reliable and consistent, regardless of the business discipline.<br>
<br>
Additionally, Natural Factors must adhere to stringent quality control systems including method validation, stability program, and data accountability. Many features of SYSPRO, such as lot traceability, have improved quality control and quality assurances processes. <br>
<br>
Shortcomings<br>
Trading between companies in SYSPRO is not as smooth as it could be. As Natural Factors expands, it has chosen to go the multiple company route because it suits the company’s business goals. While the companies buy and sell daily, the procedures between a supplier in one company and a customer in another in SYSPRO are quite rigid in terms of definitions. Natural Factors would like to see an easy way of simultaneously processing a purchase order (P/O) and a sales order (S/O) across companies.<br>
<br>
Overall evaluation <br>
When Natural Factors built its state-of-the-art manufacturing facility in Coquitlam, British Columbia, Canada, it knew it would use SYSPRO as its software package and leverage it as much as possible. The company has been pleasantly surprised with the scalability of the SYSPRO software and its ability to adapt when needed. SYSPRO enables Natural Factors to focus on the real business issues of getting its natural health care product formulations out to the market, and the company is happy with the results.<br>
<br>
Jaime De Sequera is chief information officer at Natural Factors Nutritional Products (NFNP). He brings to NFNP a wealth of experience with various software packages including SAP, BPICS, and J.D. Edwards. <br>
