Vendor Comments<br>
Since its inception in 1978, SYSPRO has been delivering state-of-the-art business software solutions to a broad range of customers that include some of the world’s most prestigious companies. Today SYSPRO, with offices worldwide, has sold its software to more than 6,000 companies in 50 countries. SYSPRO software is a complete, best-of-breed solution.<br>
<br>
SYSPRO 6.0 has built-in core functionality for an integrated, end-to-end supply chain solution, including ERP, CRM, APS, e-commerce and warehouse management. New in SYSPRO 6.0 are business analytics, document flow management, integrated CRM, and finite scheduling, among other outstanding features. SYSPRO e.net solutions forms the foundation of SYSPRO 6.0. The component-based architecture is designed to provide a highly cost-effective way for SYSPRO customers to integrate best-of-breed applications, maximize business-to-business trading, and leverage wireless connectivity. It also provides the framework for a new generation of Web-based applications. These new applications developed using Microsoft ASP.NET and Microsoft .NET architecture are fully customizable to meet customer requirements. The Document Flow Manager, a SYSPRO e.net solutions tool, enables electronic processing of inter-company and business-to-business transactions (including simultaneous purchase order (P/O) and sales order (S/O) processing). <br>
<br>
SYSPRO CRM closes the gap between the front office and the back office by integrating all activities without duplicating input. With SYSPRO CRM, sales, marketing, and customer support operations work collaboratively to achieve total customer satisfaction. SYSPRO CRM offers powerful synchronization features and Web tools to facilitate remote and off-line access via browser, laptop, and Web-enabled portable or handheld personal digital assistant (PDA) devices.<br>
<br>
SYSPRO advanced planning and scheduling (APS) enables managers to determine actual lead times, answer “what-if” questions instantly, and feed an order into the production schedule in seconds enabling businesses to operate with renewed confidence.<br>
<br>
The SYSPRO APS application suite is used to enhance existing manufacturing systems, effectively closing the loop between material requirements planning (MRP)/enterprise resources planning (ERP) business functions and the shop floor. In this way, SYSPRO APS addresses the primary weakness of contemporary manufacturing management systems: their inability to give managers useful, real-time information on current shop floor activities. Now, factory managers can continue to use their existing manufacturing management system to control sales and marketing, manage the supply chain, and balance batch efficiencies. They can also use the rapid scheduling and order tracking power of SYSPRO APS to cope with volatile changes in demand and pinpoint individual customer preferences in the production schedule. </span><br>
